 lines.append(f'Actual request timing from the09:38Z account read: the current MiniPekka request has0/2 received, with next request approximately16:07Z on17October. If the recommended target is requested then and fully granted each cycle, the last required request opens approximately{unlock:%Y-%m-%d %H:%M UTC}; the upgrade unlocks when its donations arrive. No unreceived copies are counted. Latest09:40:41Z read confirms unchanged levels, copies and budgets. Both known gold shop offers are already purchased; no additional offer is assumed.')
 if first['ci'][0]<=0:lines.append('The first target’s pooled95% interval includes zero. The recommendation uses the point estimate and request time; a win-rate improvement is not established at95%.')
 copy_order=sorted(ranked,key=lambda r:r['pp_per_missing_copy'],reverse=True);time_order=sorted(ranked,key=lambda r:r['clan_requests']);request_eff=sorted(ranked,key=lambda r:r['pp_per_request_cycle'],reverse=True)
 lines += ['Pooled Δ point order: '+' → '.join(r['card'] for r in ranked)+'.', 'Δ per missing copy point order: '+' → '.join(r['card'] for r in copy_order)+'.', 'Fastest initial unlock order: '+' → '.join(r['card'] for r in time_order)+'. Equal request counts are ties.', 'Δ per initial request-cycle point order: '+' → '.join(r['card'] for r in request_eff)+'.']
 strong=lookup[first['candidate'],'strong opponent'];lines.append(f'First target by opponent: R3a {interval(lookup[first["candidate"],"R3a"])} pp; strong LIVE-K4CW-r16 {interval(strong)} pp. Strong-opponent uncertainty is shown separately.')
 lines+=['|Singleton|Pooled Δ pp [95% CI]|Strong Δ pp [95% CI]|R3a Δ pp [95% CI]|Missing after wilds|Requests|Hours (first now / after7h)|Pooled pp/missing copy [95% CI]|','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for r in ranked:
  ac=next(x for x in inventory['rows'] if x['card']==r['card']);eff=r['pp_per_missing_copy_ci'];lines.append(f'|{r["card"]} {ac["from_level"]}→{ac["to_level"]}|{interval(r)}|{interval(lookup[r["candidate"],"strong opponent"])}|{interval(lookup[r["candidate"],"R3a"])}|{r["missing_copies"]} {r["rarity"].lower()}|{r["clan_requests"]}|{r["clan_hours_first_request_now"]}/{r["clan_hours_next_request_in7h"]}|{r["pp_per_missing_copy"]:+.3f} [{eff[0]:+.3f}, {eff[1]:+.3f}]|')
 lines+=['Each initial gap/time row allocates all currently available wild cards of that rarity to that singleton. Those are alternatives. Request income assumes one request every7hours, granting2rare or8common copies. Slot-based times assume prompt grants; donation delays can extend them. Missing-copy efficiency is not gem ROI. There are no gem shop offers for deck-card copies. Daily gold offers and chests may shorten waits; no arrival rates are assumed. Valkyrie9/20 is confirmed.','|Sequential priority|Missing after remaining wild stock|Requests|Wilds actually redeemed after full grants|Gold|','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for r in order:lines.append(f'|{r["card"]}|{r["missing_copies_sequential"]}|{r["requests_sequential"]}|{r["wild_allocated"]} {r["rarity"].lower()}|{r["gold"]:,}|')
 grant=2 if first['rarity']=='Rare' else 8;copies=first['requests_sequential']*grant;left=inventory['gold']-first['gold'];wild=dict(inventory['wild_cards']);wild[first['rarity'].lower()]-=first['wild_allocated']
 lines.append(f'Conditional first upgrade after those request grants: {a["card"]} {a["from_level"]}→{a["to_level"]}, {a["gold"]:,} gold; held{a["held_copies"]} + requested{copies} + {first["wild_allocated"]} {a["rarity"].lower()} wilds. Remaining gold{left:,}, common wilds{wild["common"]}, rare wilds{wild["rare"]}, gems425 unchanged, before intervening income. Redeem wilds after copies arrive, so whole-request rounding does not waste them. No purchase/request/upgrade executed by this worker.')
 allplus=lookup['all-plus1','pooled'];baseline=lookup['baseline','pooled'];lines += [f'All eight deck cards+1 at fixed King7: pooled {interval(allplus)} pp. Baseline {baseline["wins"]}/{baseline["n"]} wins; all+1 {allplus["wins"]}/{allplus["n"]}. This is not divided by eight or treated as the sum of singleton effects.',f'Complete measured audit:1600games,200paired cases (100 R3a/100strong), {audit["search_decisions"]} search decisions, zero genuine failures/cutoffs. Reserve serial full-pool twin, native1/pool0/chunks4 with f1a2 and no wall deadline; deployed all-L11 planner handling retained. Our truth levels Valkyrie6/Archers8/Bats7/Cannon7/Fireball6/Zap6/MiniPekka7/Giant7; King7. Singletons change only the named card.',f'Measured population:14battles, actual opponent trophies1815–2000 (mean1895.14),109 identified card slots for rarity-specific level draws; all112 displayed levels retained for pooled missing-rarity fallback. Three null identities never inferred. Independent King draws13×8/1×9. Original91 true opponent decks/seeds/seat/permutations are unchanged; this is a level-prior update, not a new arena deck-frequency sample.', 'CIs:20,000 paired percentile bootstrap resamples within policy, identical case indices across arms; pooled gives equal weight to the two policies. Draws count as nonwins. Intervals are pointwise, without multiplicity adjustment or prior/simulator/model uncertainty. Ranking selected point estimates is exploratory. Absolute simulated win rates are not ladder forecasts.',f'Measured bank SHA `{audit["bank_sha256"]}`. Source population SHA `{meta["prior"]["source_sha256"]}`. Truth RoyaleSim0.1.34/client16.402; runtime live16402b-r3 native SHA `de11f12401da396b309cd2e5d3ea422cfa1c94f462a4e3250fd51d89a62887b1`; frozen source1a65dcd1a00c5e3f891228df878d3bbebe4de187. Full metadata and original shifted results remain in REPORT.md; raw data stay private.']
 if (ROOT/'PRIOR-COMPARISON.md').exists():lines += [(ROOT/'PRIOR-COMPARISON.md').read_text()]
 (ROOT/'TARGET.md').write_text('\n\n'.join(lines).replace('|\n\n|','|\n|').rstrip()+'\n')
 print(json.dumps(dict(first_target=first['card'],pooled=interval(first),strong=interval(strong),order=[r['card'] for r in order])))
